Getting Started with Algebra,7,"Begin the year, communicate about algebra, represent patterns, introduce variables and basic equations.","CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.SSE.A.1, CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.CED.A.1"
Equations and Problem Solving,13,"Write, stack, and solve equations (including one-step and multi-step); apply order of operations; model real situations.","CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.CED.A.1, CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.REI.A.1"
Linear Equations and Representations,11,Write and solve linear equations; graph lines; create tables & graphs from linear functions; interpret solutions contextually.,"CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.CED.A.2, CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.REI.B.3"
Systems of Equations,8,"Write, solve, and apply systems of equations (graphically and algebraically); standard and real-world forms.","CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.REI.C.5, CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.REI.C.6"
Function Families and Graphs,17,"Understand and use function families: linear, exponential, quadratic; create tables & graphs; convert between forms; identify features of functions.","CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSF.IF.A.1, CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSF.IF.C.7, CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSF.IF.C.8"
Exponents Factors and Polynomials,10,"Generalize properties of exponents; find GCF & factors (numeric and algebraic); multiply polynomials, factor and simplify expressions.","CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.SSE.A.2, CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.APR.A.1"
Quadratics: Vertex & Factored Forms,10,Model with quadratics in vertex and factored form; use graphs/tables; relate to real situations; convert between standard and factored forms.,"CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSA.REI.B.4, CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSF.IF.C.8"
Functions in Context and Synthesis,8,Apply linear and exponential functions to real-world situations; describe and analyze graphs; use representations and interpret features.,CCSS.MATH.CONTENT.HSF.IF.C.9
Assessment Review and Synthesis,6,"District/interim assessments, midterms, state practice exams, and cumulative reviews; performance tasks; closing activities.",All above
